    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20028" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gurgustĭum</span></b> , ii, n.
		kindred with gurgulio, perh. with reference to its
		straitness, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small</i>, <i>mean dwelling</i>, <i>a hovel</i>, <i>hut</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nescio quo e gurgustio te prodire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 6, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in gurgustio habitare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					N. D. 1, 9, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">modicum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Gramm. 11</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ambros. de Bono Mort. 1, 5
		al.</span></i></div>
